I disagree, I think there's plenty of room for new features in
Nethack.  Nethack got to be the way it is by adding new features to
Hack, which got to where it was by adding on to Rogue.  Slash'EM
includes lots of new features, some a little too extreme for me. 
(Lightsabers, ugh.)  But then again, I think vanilla Nethack has too
many "random effect" features (fountains, sinks, thrones) that have
one or two outcomes that are a bit too lethal.

I agree that many of ADOM's features aren't so hot.  Quests, story
lines and alternate endings are of dubious value to a Roguelike. 
Ditto "characters," I think Nethack's got it exactly right in that
regard.  I really like the Conway's Life-style herbs in ADOM, and the
small cave dungeon is a neat idea, but overall it seems unfocused and
spurious.  And despite superficially adding more dungeons, most of
them aren't that different from each other.

I think a lot of ADOM's problems come from it being almost entirely
the work of one person.  If Nethack's source code were locked up and
out of sight, we'd have many fewer spoilers, and many fewer winners,
than we have now.

